---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ReviewsRail from '../../components/ReviewsRail.astro';

const PAGE_URL = 'https://ka-performancefl.com/locations/jacksonville/';

// Home > Jacksonville. No /locations/ index exists on purpose, so the trail
// has exactly two crumbs and both of them resolve.
const breadcrumb = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://ka-performancefl.com/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Jacksonville', item: PAGE_URL },
  ],
};

const services = [
  {
    href: '/services/web-design/',
    kicker: 'Web design',
    blurb: 'A site built for your business from scratch, reviewed on a real staging URL.',
  },
  {
    href: '/services/ai-integration/',
    kicker: 'AI integration',
    blurb: 'Assistants, automations, and AI audio, built into the site rather than bolted on.',
  },
  {
    href: '/services/seo-ai-search/',
    kicker: 'SEO & AI search',
    blurb: 'A competitive market needs links and reviews too. We say so, then do our half.',
  },
  {
    href: '/services/accessibility/',
    kicker: 'Accessibility',
    blurb: 'Contrast, keyboard paths, screen readers. Checked, not claimed.',
  },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Web Design in Jacksonville, FL | K & A Performance"
  description="Web design and AI integration for Jacksonville businesses, run remote on purpose. Live client work in Jax, a Jacksonville-based artist, and free project quotes."
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline set:html={JSON.stringify(breadcrumb)} />

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 pt-40 pb-16 md:pt-48">
    <p data-animate="type-settle" class="font-mono text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-muted">
      Jacksonville, Florida
    </p>
    <h1 data-animate="type-settle" data-animate-delay="0.1" class="mt-6 font-display text-[clamp(2.25rem,6vw,4.5rem)] leading-[1.04]">
      Web design in Jacksonville, <span class="text-accent">remote on purpose</span>
    </h1>
    <p data-animate="type-settle" data-animate-delay="0.2" class="mt-8 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
      We are not going to pretend there is a Jacksonville office. The studio is
      in Gainesville, about two hours down the road, and everything we have
      shipped in Jacksonville got built over shared links, recorded
      walkthroughs, and a staging site the client could open at midnight. That
      is the honest version, and so far it has not cost anybody anything.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl border-t border-ink/10 px-6 py-20 md:py-24">
    <h2 data-animate="type-settle" class="font-display text-3xl leading-tight md:text-5xl">We have already built here</h2>
    <p data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-6 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Fore Motion Golf, one of the builds in the gallery on our
      <a href="/" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent-hot">home page</a>,
      is indoor golf in Jacksonville: always 70 degrees, always sunny, whatever
      August is doing outside. Their launch site had one job before the doors
      opened, which was to turn interest into a founding-membership waitlist, so
      the whole thing is built around that capture. It runs dark and moody
      because the room does, and it ships with an AI Robo Caddie visitors can
      actually talk to.
    </p>
    <p data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      It is a fair example of what remote looks like when it works. What the
      project needed was somebody who understood a membership launch, not
      somebody who could park in the same lot.
    </p>
    <p data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Fore Motion is not alone here either. Southern Legacy Contractors and
      Synovial Marketing are both Jacksonville businesses running on K &amp; A
      builds, and PB&amp;J Strategic Accounting is just down the road in
      Fleming Island. All of it in the gallery on the home page, all of it
      built remote from Gainesville.
    </p>

    <h2 data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-16 font-display text-3xl leading-tight md:text-5xl">Nicole is Jacksonville</h2>
    <p data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-6 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      The artist we commission for brand identity and merchandise design lives
      and works here, and her portfolio makes it obvious. Jax Beach Softball,
      the Jax Beach Thunder All Stars, team identity and challenge coins and
      apparel for organisations across the First Coast. If a project needs a
      mark that has to survive being embroidered on a jersey, struck into metal,
      or carried around a tournament all weekend, that is a different discipline
      from picking a typeface, and it is hers.
    </p>
    <p data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      She is commissioned and art directed through us, so a Jacksonville client
      who needs both a site and a mark gets one point of contact for the pair.
      Her work is on
      <a href="/artists/nicole/" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent-hot">Nicole's page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-16 font-display text-3xl leading-tight md:text-5xl">How remote actually runs</h2>
    <p data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-6 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      There is a version of remote that means slow email and a surprise at the
      end. This is not that. You get a live staging URL early, so you are never
      approving a picture of a website, and feedback happens on the real thing
      on your own phone. Walkthroughs get recorded and sent, which you can watch
      at 6am instead of holding a meeting that a link would have covered.
      Questions get a reply within 24 hours.
    </p>
    <p data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      And the drive is two hours, not two time zones. For a kickoff worth doing
      in a room, we will make it. Remote is also exactly how
      <a href="/ai-launch/" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent-hot">the 90-Day AI Launch</a>
      runs: weekly video sessions that end with AI doing a real job inside
      your business.
    </p>

    <h2 data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-16 font-display text-3xl leading-tight md:text-5xl">Fleming Island, Orange Park, St. Augustine</h2>
    <p data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-6 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Jacksonville is several markets wearing one name, and the searches do not
      behave the same way in each of them. A Fleming Island or Orange Park
      business is usually competing for the people who already live nearby and
      want a reason to stop driving north. St. Augustine is full of visitors
      searching on a phone while standing in the street, which is a different
      page with a different first screen. We write them as separate briefs
      rather than swapping a town name into the same paragraph, because the
      person doing the searching wants a different thing in each one.
    </p>
    <p data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Worth saying plainly: Jacksonville is a bigger, harder market than our
      home one, and on-page work alone will not carry you to the top of it.
      Reviews and real local links matter more here than anywhere else we work,
      and we will tell you that before you hire us rather than after.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl border-t border-ink/10 px-6 py-20 md:py-24">
    <h2 data-animate="type-settle" class="font-display text-3xl leading-tight md:text-5xl">What we do for Jacksonville clients</h2>
    <p data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-6 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-muted">
      The same four things we do everywhere, scoped to what the business
      actually needs.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2">
      {services.map((s) => (
        <a href={s.href} data-animate="frame-lift" class="glow-frame group flex flex-col p-7">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-accent">{s.kicker}</p>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">{s.blurb}</p>
          <p class="mt-5 font-heading text-sm font-semibold tracking-wide text-accent">
            Read more <span class="inline-block transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-1" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
          </p>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p data-animate="type-settle" class="mt-10 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Closer to the studio? The in-person version of all this is on the
      <a href="/locations/gainesville/" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent-hot">Gainesville page</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="border-t border-ink/10">
    <ReviewsRail />
  </div>

  <section class="px-6 pb-40 pt-16 md:pt-24">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl text-center">
      <p data-animate="type-settle" class="font-display text-[clamp(2.25rem,5.5vw,4.5rem)] leading-[1.05]">
        Send us the <span class="text-accent">rough idea</span>
      </p>
      <p data-animate="type-settle" data-animate-delay="0.1" class="mx-auto mt-8 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
        A competitor you envy, a site you already hate, or three lines about
        what the business does. We will come back with what it would take, what
        it would cost, and whether it is worth building.
      </p>
      <div data-animate="type-settle" data-animate-delay="0.2" class="mt-10">
        <a href="/contact/" class="btn-accent">Start a project</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
